From 256b7610d2f773b8b476d764fc44db31df736bd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arodrigues-puc-rio <arodrigues@puc-rio.br>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 09:26:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(reward): close PBRS reward-farming loophole in
 capture_v0_pure_potential_shaping

Eval of the PBRS-trained policy showed all ghosts collapsing to 2-cell
oscillations and ignoring a visible, stationary Pacman 3 cells away for 40+
steps - banking +17.5 shaping (=+50 team) over 80 steps with zero captures.

Root cause: discounted telescoping (gamma=0.99) with Phi<=0 pays
(1-gamma)*(-Phi)>0 per back-and-forth cycle, and the 'two nearest ghosts'
team distance is discontinuous (nearest-ghost identity swaps), producing
large non-cancelling per-step swings. Together they made camping profitable.

Fix: exact (gamma=1) telescoping F = Phi(s') - Phi(s) over the smooth MIN
ghost distance, so cumulative shaping = Phi(end)-Phi(start) is path-independent
and any in-place oscillation nets exactly 0; stronger timestep -0.05 so camping
is strictly negative. Verified: an 80-step camp now nets -3.3 (was +50.1).
Added regression test test_pure_pbrs_in_place_oscillation_cannot_be_farmed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
